               <desc>A distinct configuration of the platform edition’s mechanics and gameplay in the gameplay footage</desc>
               <desc>Note that <q>Default</q> and <q>Normal / moderate</q> are separate options. Select <q>Default</q> if only one gameplay mode is available or the default gameplay mode does not have a unique name or identifier. Select <q>Normal / moderate</q> if that gameplay mode was selected among other options, such as <q>Hard / expert</q> and <q>Easy / beginner / casual.</q>
               </desc>
               <desc>Controlled vocabulary adapted, with minor changes, from Wikipedia, "Glossary of Video Game Terms," 2026</desc>
