            <elementSpec ident="progressionTrope" module="PressRecord">
               <gloss>Progression Trope</gloss>
               <desc>
                  <q>A generally recognizable [progression] device or [level design] convention [appearing in the footage]. [Progression] tropes rely on culturally mediated expectations to expedite [advancement, acknowledge attempts to advance, or afford players with a sense of progress, achievement, or productivity]. When overused or oversimplified, tropes often come at the expense of fair and inclusive representations</q> (Lee et al., <q>VGMS 4.2,</q> 2024).</desc>
               <desc>This element will typically be repeated. It differs from the <q>Narrative Trope</q> element, which focuses on diegetic events and actions, by focusing on devices and conventions that influence or shape players’ decision-making. These devices and conventions often prompt non-diegetic actions.</desc>
               <desc>See TV Tropes for definitions and examples of many tropes in this controlled vocabulary. The use of TV Tropes should be accompanied by peer-reviewed scholarship in Media and Game Studies.</desc>
